"Edges: A→B 4, A→C 1, C→B 2, B→D 1, C→D 5. From A: dist A=0, C=1, B=min(4,1+2)=3, D=min(3+1,1+5)=4. Shortest A→D = 4 via A–C–B–D.",
["Single-source shortest path; weights ≥ 0.","Greedy: pick unvisited vertex with the smallest distance.","Relaxation: if d[u]+w < d[v] update d[v].","O(V²) with array; O((V+E) log V) with min-heap.","Fails with negative edges (use Bellman–Ford).","Path recovered via parent pointers."],
